<.docs_layout active_guide={@guide.slug}>
  <.guide_heading guide={@guide} />

  <section class="mt-10 space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-medium tracking-tight">Three durations</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
      Motion confirms an action or orients a transition - it never decorates.
      Easing is <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs">ease</code>
      / <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs">ease-out</code>;
      animate only opacity and transform.
    </p>
    <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-base-300">
      <table class="table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th class="w-36">Tier</th>
            <th class="w-28">Duration</th>
            <th>Properties</th>
            <th>Examples</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr :for={
            {tier, dur, props, ex} <- [
              {"micro", "150ms", "color, bg, border, shadow", "button hover / active"},
              {"small surface", "180ms", "opacity, transform", "popover, tooltip, ⌘K palette"},
              {"large surface", "300ms", "translate, backdrop", "sheet, drawer"},
              {"chip in / out", "150ms", "scale, opacity, translate",
               "chip row chips and their neighbours"},
              {"row reveal", "180ms", "grid-template-rows, opacity",
               "filter chip row, inline alert, accordion"},
              {"theme switch", "0ms", "-", "instant by design"}
            ]
          }>
            <td class="font-medium">{tier}</td>
            <td class="font-mono text-xs">{dur}</td>
            <td class="font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground">{props}</td>
            <td class="text-muted-foreground">{ex}</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
      Try them live: hover any button (micro), open the <kbd class="kbd kbd-sm">⌘K</kbd>
      palette (small surface), or the
      <a href={~p"/docs/components/drawer"} class="link link-primary">drawer</a>
      component (large surface).
    </p>

    <div class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3">
      <div
        :for={
          {tier, dur} <- [
            {"micro", 150},
            {"small surface", 180},
            {"large surface", 300}
          ]
        }
        class="space-y-3 rounded-lg border border-base-300 p-4"
      >
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <span class="text-sm font-medium">{tier}</span>
          <span class="font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground">{dur}ms</span>
        </div>
        <div class="relative h-9 overflow-hidden rounded-md bg-muted">
          <div
            data-motion-box
            class="absolute left-1 top-1 flex size-7 items-center justify-center rounded bg-primary text-primary-foreground"
          >
            <span class="hero-arrow-right size-4" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <%!-- Web Animations API: unaffected by the theme-swap transition-duration override. --%>
        <button
          type="button"
          class="btn btn-outline btn-sm w-full"
          data-motion-play={dur}
        >
          Replay {dur}ms
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12 space-y-4" data-platform="web">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-medium tracking-tight">The patch guard - don't fight it</h2>
    <div class="rounded-lg border border-base-300 bg-muted/40 px-4 py-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
      <p>
        Theme switching is instant by design: fading light↔dark passes text through a grey
        crossover where contrast dies. While <code class="font-mono text-xs">&lt;html&gt;</code>
        carries the <code class="font-mono text-xs">theme-transition</code>
        class, the theme CSS forces <code class="font-mono text-xs">transition-duration: 0s</code>
        on everything except components with their own enter/exit animations (dialog, drawer,
        tooltip, carousel, skeleton, countdown). <code class="font-mono text-xs">setTheme</code>
        from <code class="font-mono text-xs">shadcn-daisyui.js</code>
        adds the class, swaps <code class="font-mono text-xs">data-theme</code>, and drops it on
        the next frame, so hover/focus/micro transitions stay live the rest of the time. Setting
        <code class="font-mono text-xs">data-theme</code>
        directly skips the guard and the swap fades.
      </p>
    </div>
    <ul class="list-inside list-disc space-y-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
      <li>No entrance animations for page content - skeletons cover loading.</li>
      <li>
        Never animate layout properties (width, height, top/left, margin) - except the
        row reveal below.
      </li>
      <li>
        Gate any added animation behind <code class="font-mono text-xs">prefers-reduced-motion</code>.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12 space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-medium tracking-tight">Collapsing rows</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
      A row that appears and disappears in the page flow (active filter chips, an inline
      alert, a bulk-action bar) may slide open and closed:
      <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs">grid-template-rows</code>
      0fr ↔ 1fr plus opacity, 180ms ease-out, instant under reduced motion. It's the one
      sanctioned layout animation, and what the accordion already does. Use <a
        href={~p"/docs/components/reveal"}
        class="link link-primary"
      >&lt;.reveal open&gt;</a>; never
      hand-animate height or max-height.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
      Keep the row's content rendered and let <code class="font-mono text-xs">open</code>
      drive it: chips in a
      <a href={~p"/docs/components/chip-row"} class="link link-primary">chip row</a>
      scale and fade in and out (150ms) while the reveal grows or shrinks, so removing the
      last chip closes the row around it as one motion.
    </p>
    <div class="space-y-3 rounded-lg border border-base-300 p-4">
      <button
        type="button"
        class="btn btn-outline btn-sm"
        data-reveal-toggle="motion-reveal"
        aria-expanded="false"
      >
        Toggle row
      </button>
      <div id="motion-reveal" class="reveal">
        <div class="reveal-track">
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 pb-1">
            <span class="badge badge-secondary">Status: Todo</span>
            <span class="badge badge-secondary">Label: Bug</span>
            <span class="badge badge-secondary">Assignee: Me</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Content below moves with the row.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12 space-y-3" data-platform="ios">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-medium tracking-tight">iOS / SwiftUI</h2>
    <div class="rounded-lg border border-base-300 bg-muted/40 px-4 py-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
      <p>
        The Swift package's <code class="font-mono text-xs">Motion</code>
        presets mirror the
        tiers: <code class="font-mono text-xs">.micro</code>
        (0.15s), <code class="font-mono text-xs">.surface</code>
        (0.18s), <code class="font-mono text-xs">.sheet</code>
        (0.30s) as ease-out curves. Prefer
        system presentation animations for sheets and covers; avoid springs with visible
        overshoot; respect <code class="font-mono text-xs">accessibilityReduceMotion</code>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</.docs_layout>
